  m_Name: Axes
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  playerLines:
  - I still barely know what a coordinate is
  - I only really think of vectors as just a pair of numbers
  - Nothing special
  - <i>hmm...</i>
  - <i>So vectors operate on different axes</i>
  - <i>The number of components a vector has affects the axes it operates on</i>
  NPCLines:
  - "The concept of the coordinate was born with the conception of Cartesian coordinates
    by Ren\xE9 Descartes"
  - This led to the birth of the vector space in cartesian coordinates
  - Vectors are the building blocks of vector spaces, able to express anythin point
    in said space
  - Vectors are important as they allow the perception of numbers in different directions
  - The Cartesian coordinates operate on what we know as the standard basis
  - The ability of vectors to have different numerical components in separate axes
    is vital
  speakTurnPlayer: 01000000010100000001
